WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.423
Every school year, new
students, transferees,

2
00:00:03.473 --> 00:00:07.940
and visitors walk through the gates
of Notre Dame of Marbel University.

3
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.840
It's a big campus, full of buildings,
offices, and places to discover.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.100
But finding your way isn't always easy.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.930
Most newcomers have to ask
around, or rely on signs.

6
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.315
So our study set out to build three
things: an augmented reality campus tour,

7
00:00:26.365 --> 00:00:30.850
AR assisted navigation, and one
place for campus information.

8
00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:36.023
Meet ExploreNDMU.

9
00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:40.543
An Android app built with Unity,
AR Foundation, and ARCore.

10
00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:44.873
It works fully offline, and it greets
you with a quick tour of what it can do.

11
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:51.113
Looking for an office?

12
00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:52.793
Open the directory.

13
00:00:52.843 --> 00:00:57.833
Search, or browse by category, and
read each place's details and services.

14
00:00:57.963 --> 00:01:02.133
Save the places you visit often,
so they're always one tap away.

15
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:08.283
Now, let's go to the Library.

16
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:11.773
Tap Navigate here, and choose
where you're starting from.

17
00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:13.773
Then, lift your phone.

18
00:01:14.023 --> 00:01:18.140
Gold arrows appear on the ground
through your camera, showing the way,

19
00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.463
step by step.

20
00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:21.215
A voice tells you when to turn,

21
00:01:21.265 --> 00:01:24.283
and the screen shows how
far you have left to go.

22
00:01:24.443 --> 00:01:25.643
No map reading.

23
00:01:25.693 --> 00:01:27.703
No need to ask for directions.

24
00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.343
Just follow the arrows.

25
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.971
When you arrive, a gold
pin marks your destination,

26
00:01:46.021 --> 00:01:49.553
and an info card tells you
about the place in front of you.

27
00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:56.043
New to campus?

28
00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:58.963
Start a guided tour from
any of the four gates.

29
00:01:59.213 --> 00:02:03.833
The app leads you from stop to stop, and
you can skip a stop whenever you like.

30
00:02:06.783 --> 00:02:11.523
Scan a printed marker, and the
university's statues appear in 3D.

31
00:02:11.813 --> 00:02:16.143
Mother Mary, Saint Marcellin
Champagnat, and the Bronze Stallion.

32
00:02:16.393 --> 00:02:19.783
Walk around them, and see
every detail up close.

33
00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:27.773
How does it work?

34
00:02:27.823 --> 00:02:30.703
Our team walked the campus
routes and recorded them.

35
00:02:30.953 --> 00:02:32.534
The app joins these paths,

36
00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:35.420
and uses Dijkstra's
shortest path algorithm to

37
00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.103
find the best way to your destination.

38
00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:42.045
Everything lives inside the app,
so newcomers can find their way,

39
00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.444
get information in one place,
and reach where they're going,

40
00:02:45.494 --> 00:02:47.443
without asking for directions.

41
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:01.343
ExploreNDMU.

42
00:03:01.393 --> 00:03:03.553
Your campus, in your hands.

43
00:03:03.663 --> 00:03:04.543
Explore.

44
00:03:04.593 --> 00:03:05.433
Navigate.

45
00:03:05.483 --> 00:03:06.933
Discover.
